Computer hardware means all the physical parts of a computer. These are the parts that we can see and touch. For example, a computer has a screen,
 keyboard, mousem processor, memory and storage. Each part has a differend job. Hardware helps the computer receive information, process it, save data and show results.

Software is the digital part of a computer. It consists of programs and instructions that help the computer perform different tasks.
We cannot physically touch software. Some common examples are Windows, Google Chrome, games and Microsoft Word.
Differen software is designed for differens purposes, such as communication, studying, entertaiment and working with files.


Hardware and software need each other to work properly. Software tells the hardware what actions to perform. For example, when you open a program,
 the computer uses its processor and memory to run it. When you type something on a keyboard, the hardware sends the information to the software, which then processes and displays it.
